## The 6 tiers

| Tier | Use for | Example |
|---|---|---|
| command | Imperative one-liner you'd run | `ssh build-host` |
| rule | "always/never X" guardrail | "Never push to main without review" |
| skill | "when X, do Y" recipe | "When the embedder runs out of memory, enable CPU fallback" |
| entity | Canonical noun (host/service/person) | `storage-node (internal address)` |
| decision | "we chose X because Y" | "Use a smaller embedding model to fit the hardware budget" |
| episodic | Session log / reflection | Auto-extracted at session end |

## How to recall

```
hive_recall("storage host access", top_k=5)
```

Normal recall is one bounded, non-reranked pass. Use `deep=true` only when an
explicit, slower knowledge-tier sweep is worth the latency. `hive_expand(item_id,
layer="summary")` if the abstract is not enough.

## How to write

```
hive_teach(trigger="...", action="...", success_hint="...")
hive_ingest(content="...", tags=["..."])
```

Both may auto-classify when a classifier is configured. Low-confidence items land
in the review queue.

## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| 401 on any call | Missing, expired, or revoked key | Refresh the configured agent credential |
| 403 on admin op | Writer key reaching admin endpoint | Use a separately provisioned admin credential |
| Empty recall | Wrong namespace or no relevant memory | Check an authorized namespace; otherwise accept `NO_MEMORY_NEEDED` |
| Irrelevant result | Query mismatch | Rate the exact item ID with `signal="irrelevant"` |
| Stale or false stored fact | Content is wrong | Rate the exact item ID with `signal="wrong"` |
| Loadout missing | SessionStart hook timed out | Call `hive_loadout()` mid-session |

